# Copy to .env and fill in. Bun auto-loads .env for `bun run` and `bunx`.
NODE_ENV=development

# Postgres connection string. Dev uses a remote Postgres (e.g. Neon) — get the
# real URL from the team. Format (managed/SSL endpoints usually need sslmode):
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST/DBNAME?sslmode=require

# Better Auth — generate a strong secret: `openssl rand -base64 32`
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=
BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Used by the browser auth client.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Optional: set both to enable Google sign-in.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Optional: set ALL THREE to enable the Google Drive folder integration (sales
# folders on opportunities, project folders on projects, and the Files tabs).
# Setup runbook: docs/guides/google-drive.md
#
# In short: in the same Cloud project as the OAuth client above, enable the
# Drive API and the Picker API, keep the consent screen INTERNAL (that's what
# permits the restricted `drive` scope with no Google verification), and add
# https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive to the OAuth client's scopes.
#
# Note: adding the scope grants nothing retroactively — everyone must sign out
# and back in once before Drive works for them, because Google only issues the
# refresh token we need on a fresh consent.
#
# The "Lazer Home" SHARED DRIVE id (from its URL: /drive/folders/<id>). Point
# dev at a SEPARATE shared drive — that's why there's no `test-` name prefix
# here, unlike Slack, where one workspace has to serve both.
# GOOGLE_DRIVE_ROOT_ID=
# Picker credentials, both public by design. The API key should be restricted
# to the Picker API; the app id is the Cloud project NUMBER.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_PICKER_API_KEY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_PICKER_APP_ID=

# Optional: set to enable the Slack channel integration (scoping/project
# channels on opportunities and projects). Setup runbook: docs/guides/slack.md
#
# In short: create a Slack app, install it to the workspace, and give the BOT
# token these scopes — channels:read, groups:read, channels:manage, groups:write,
# users:read.email. The token starts with `xoxb-` (a `xoxp-` user token is
# rejected at boot). Restart the app after setting it; env is parsed once.
#
# Note: the bot can only see PRIVATE channels it has been added to, so an
# existing scoping channel must be `/invite`d before it can be found and linked.
# Channels created outside production are prefixed `test-`.
# SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=
# Optional: scopes Slack deep links to one workspace (find it in a Slack URL).
# SLACK_TEAM_ID=
